    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0066","sequence":78,
      "meaning":"Every river flows with pure water, and birds, animals and bees live happily. All creatures abandon their natural enmity and cherish the mountain. With Girijā’s arrival, the mountain glows like a person who has attained devotion to Rāma; ever-new auspiciousness fills the house of her whose glory Brahmā and the gods sing. Hearing all the news, Nārada comes to the mountain king’s home out of delighted curiosity. The king honors him greatly, washes his feet and offers an excellent seat. With his wife, he bows his head at the sage’s feet and sprinkles the whole dwelling with the foot-water. After describing his great good fortune, he summons his daughter and places her at the sage’s feet. He asks the eminent, omniscient knower of all three times, whose movement reaches everywhere, to consider and reveal his daughter’s faults and virtues.",
