    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0068","sequence":80,
      "meaning":"Knowing the sage’s words to be true, the royal couple grieve while Umā rejoices. Even Nārada does not know this secret: the same condition is understood differently. Girijā, her companions, Himālaya and Mainā all thrill bodily and fill their eyes with tears. The divine sage’s speech cannot be false, so Umā preserves it in her heart. Love for Śiva’s lotus feet arises, though she doubts whether union with him can be attained. Knowing the moment unsuitable, she hides her love and returns to sit in a companion’s lap. The couple and their wise companions worry because the divine sage’s words cannot prove false. Gathering courage, the mountain king asks what remedy is possible. Nārada answers that no god, demon, human, nāga or sage can erase what fate has written upon the forehead.",
