    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0070","sequence":82,
      "meaning":"Saints know liquor made from Ganges water to be liquor and never drink it; yet once it merges into the Ganges it becomes pure like her. Such is the difference between the Lord and one who is not the Lord. Śambhu is innately mighty and divine, so this marriage brings welfare in every way. Maheśa is difficult to propitiate, yet when austerity is practiced he is Āśutoṣa, quickly pleased. If their daughter undertakes austerity, Tripurāri can erase even destiny. Though the world contains many bridegrooms, none other than Śiva is for her. He grants boons, removes the distress of those who bow, is an ocean of compassion and delights his servants’ hearts. Without worshiping Śiva, the desired fruit cannot be gained through millions of yogic, recitative or ascetic disciplines. Saying this, Nārada remembers Hari, blesses Girijā, and tells Giriśa to abandon doubt because this will bring welfare.",
